            <ArticleTitle>Phantom limb pain during spinal anaesthesia. Recurrence in amputees.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>886-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Phantom limb pain following amputation is a well known but comparatively rare phenomenon. Spinal anaesthesia in amputees may cause reappearance of phantom pain in previously pain-free patients despite complete sensory analgesia. Two such cases are described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
